		(uuid "09b68ffe-b842-4242-8b6f-662e5930e3d5")
	)
	(text "TN panel pin 1 = X- (touch) ('FPC' column of notes/screens.md). Check the FPC contact side (FH12 = bottom contact) against the panel before ordering."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 203.2 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "14b53091-d4de-4694-af94-b856e29d9593")
	)
	(text "Backlight anode: +3.3V (1-2, default) or VSYS (2-3)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 88.9 99.06 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "1f9eafac-cae2-418f-ba82-6ae6854ad32a")
	)
	(text "- Data: TFT_D0-D7 = PC0-PC7 (low byte lane), TFT_D8-D15 = PD8-PD15 (high byte lane). TFT_DC = PD0, TFT_WR = PD1.\n- One chip select per panel: TFT_CS1 = PB8 (TN), TFT_CS2 = PB9 (IPS). Never drive both low.\n- RDX tied to the panel rail (we never read back), RESX on NRST, TE/FMARK unused.\n- Both panels stay powered while the bus runs (no load switch: an unpowered panel would be back-powered by the bus).\n  The JP drain jumpers are only for measuring. Idle = backlight off + Display OFF / Sleep In.\n- 16-bit 8080: IM0-IM2 low on both panels. Unused serial input (SDI / SDA) tied low, SDO open."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 48.26 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "474ac524-3184-4a14-a854-9a2b893e51d4")
	)
	(text "Constant-current sink, gated by TFT_BL (TIM2 PWM above 20 kHz):\nI = 3.3 V x 1k / (56k + 1k) / 1R = ~58 mA while the PWM is high.\nFit C206 (1u) to filter the PWM into a DC reference: analog dimming instead."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 73.66 162.56 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "47583c49-381d-4b75-bfbf-ccb34c4bb58d")
	)
	(text "Screens: two FPC connectors on the same 16-bit 8080 bus"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 25.4 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.54 2.54)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "49c023b9-f809-4622-bbcb-35e7360483c1")
	)
	(text "Backlight anode: +3.3V (1-2, default) or VSYS (2-3)"
